-- The scaffolding is done. YOUR JOB: the stimulus process.
--
-- The DUT computes (features x1000, weights x1000, so the accumulator is
-- in the x10^6 domain):
--
--   acc = 300*f0 - 100*f1 + 200*f2 + 50000
--   acc > +10000 -> BUY  ("01")
--   acc < -10000 -> SELL ("10")
--   else         -> HOLD ("00")
--
-- Latency is 2 cycles (multiply stage, then accumulate stage).
--
-- Verify at least: one BUY, one SELL, one HOLD, and one case that uses all
-- three weights — check prediction_out, signal_out, the 2-cycle valid
-- latency, and that valid_out is a one-cycle pulse. Hint for HOLD: the
-- intercept alone is 50000 (> 10000), so HOLD needs features that pull the
-- accumulator back inside (-10000, +10000) — e.g. f0 = -150.
--
-- Grade yourself:
--   uv run pytest tests/exercises/test_05_vhdl.py -v        (needs ghdl)
--   bash scripts/run_vhdl_tests.sh tb_linear_regression_predictor
-- =============================================================================
